# What boot starts from the release's initramfs, make pi5-stage1, when
# it makes no volume /: booted with no root=, or with a volume that is
# not mounted or holds no /etc/system. The initramfs holds only the
# first stage, what mounts the disks, and this rescue shell on the debug
# UART, which boot waits for: from it, ls /Volumes, df and dmesg say
# what was found, and a card's cmdline.txt can be put right with write.
start /bin/sh
